00:42:06,800 --> 00:42:10,070
No, no, I've not. Yeah, okay.

614
00:42:10,070 --> 00:42:16,470
So, model context protocol is a way of providing an interface for an LLM to control machines.

615
00:42:16,470 --> 00:42:19,550
So, an MCP server effectively becomes a tool.

616
00:42:19,550 --> 00:42:27,590
that the LLM is aware of that it can use to interface with other machines and systems.

617
00:42:27,590 --> 00:42:30,350
Okay, so people are producing these MCP servers.

618
00:42:30,350 --> 00:42:33,950
where an LLM can control your Google Drive.

619
00:42:33,950 --> 00:42:38,230
or it can it can create issues and pull requests within a GitHub repository.

620
00:42:38,230 --> 00:42:42,590
or or it could connect to a Jira system and create tickets.

621
00:42:42,590 --> 00:42:44,830
And it's it's a very interesting technology is.

622
00:42:44,830 --> 00:42:47,350
You can see a lot of utility in this.

623
00:42:47,350 --> 00:42:55,230
where LLMs are effectively be able to autonomously interact with systems and automate these processes.

624
00:42:55,230 --> 00:42:58,990
So, they can go beyond just generating code and and engaging with a human,

625
00:42:58,990 --> 00:43:02,190
they can start to control machines.

